nger edges are  horizontal and fold it in half  lengthwise you can use scissors  or if you're good at tearing you can do  that i like to first press in the middle  and slowly line up the paper to the  right and left before i make the final  crease  we can finally fold the paper in half  one last time and then tear it when  you've done that three times your paper  will look like this  for the second piece you can keep the  other half you just tore away or use a  different color  [Music]  let's take the left side and fold it  across to the right side  hold it so that the edges are aligned  and just crease it on the left side by  just running your fingernail against  it you can open it up so that it looks  like a little mountain  and set it down on the table the right  edge  is going to go down into this vertical  line  so just line it up and then give it a  crease  on the right side here now we can take  the left side  and fold it up onto that vertical line  also making a crease on the outside here  then we could flip it over just give it  a quick press to flatten it out and  you'll notice there's a horizontal  crease here  lift up the right side so that it is  even on the bottom  with the left side as you could see here  now i'm just going to take my  fingers here my two pointers and pinch  it in the middle and set it down  on the table and i'm going to lift the  bottom edge  to the top but i'm going to leave a  little bit of space  as you'll see from here to there it's  about three to four millimeters  then you can just pinch it in the middle  with your two fingers like that  and just press down gently in the middle  making a little pinch in the paper like  this  now that we've marked the distance in  the middle we have to make sure that the  edge is the same distance and parallel  to the top one all throughout  so i'm just going to bring it up a  little closer here because i want it to  be three to four millimeters then i can  crease it all throughout the right  an